<title>USA: Crowne Ventures buys Las Vegas hotel.</title>
<headline>Crowne Ventures buys Las Vegas hotel.</headline>
<dateline>LAS VEGAS 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Crowne Ventures Inc said on Wednesday it has agreed to buy the Continental Hotel &amp; Casino located a couple of blocks from the Las Vegas strip.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement that the $35 million acquisition, which generated revenues of more than $21 million during the last audit period, substantially increases the assets and revenues of Crowne.</p>
<p>Crowne said it plans to create a nostalgia-themed resort around its wholly owned subsidiary &quot;Back To The 50's.&quot; The hotel has some 400 rooms and over 40,000 square feet of casino space.</p>
</text>
